# Larchwood Coffee Roasters — Brand health (board pack, October 2026)

## The brand is strong enough to price up

| Signal | Value | Read |
|---|---|---|
| Market position | **#1 brand, 24% market share** | Leader (market panel, H1 2026) |
| Price premium | **+23%** vs category average (EUR 38.00/kg vs EUR 30.93/kg) | Customers pay for the brand |
| NPS | **31 -> 38** (Sep 2025 -> Sep 2026) | Loyalty rising |
| Aided awareness | 60% -> 61% | Stable (change within the survey's +/-3 pt margin) |
| Customers who reorder within 90 days | 42% -> 42% (2025-Q1 vs 2026-Q2 cohorts) | Holding |
| D2C revenue Q3 | EUR 524,181, -11% vs Q2 | Seasonal: Q3 2025 was -10% vs Q2 2025; +4% year on year |

## Proposal for approval
Raise list prices by 6% on all whole-bean and ground SKUs from 1 January 2027. At flat volume this adds about EUR 141,557 revenue a year.

Sources (resources/): market_panel_2026h1.csv (syndicated panel, kg and EUR by region, channel, brand), d2c_orders_by_quarter.csv (our shop), repeat_cohorts.csv (90-day reorder by first-order quarter), brand_tracker.csv (annual tracker).
